[llm-call] glm → zai/glm-5.1
```markdown
- **`PCASIMICA`** (line 72): DD-SIMCA one-class classifier for spectral data that uses PCA, chi-squared distributions for Hotelling T² and Q-residuals, and Fisher's combined p-value test for joint acceptance.
- **`get_one_class_model`** (line 247): Factory function that returns a one-class model instance with sensible default hyperparameters for NIR data.
- **`build_one_class_model`** (line 284): Builds and returns a one-class model instance using an exact dictionary of specified hyperparameters (used primarily by search pipelines).
- **`get_one_class_model_grids`** (line 310): Returns a dictionary mapping model names to lists of predefined hyperparameter dictionaries for grid searching.
- **`one_class_metrics`** (line 353): Computes and returns a dictionary of evaluation metrics (e.g., sensitivity, specificity, AUC) for one-class classification.
- **`run_one_class_cv`** (line 404): Executes cross-validation for a specified one-class model, computing pooled metrics and fitting a final calibration model on all inliers.
- **`compute_validation_metrics_for_top_one_class_models`** (line 654): Calculates external validation metrics for the top N one-class models from a results DataFrame and appends them as new columns.
- **`compute_one_class_importances`** (line 931): Calculates feature importances for one-class data by internally treating the inlier/outlier labels as a binary classification problem.
